).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your destinations."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Where your destinations send records decides whether the data leaves the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device, and whether a third party receives it. If an endpoint you send to uses the data for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracking, your app’s manifest lists its domain under ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPrivacyTrackingDomains","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asks for permission through App Tracking Transparency first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Modules you turn off.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" If your app links a module but never turns it on, it collects nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through it, and your privacy labels can leave that data out.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"],"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"title":"CollectorEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding"},"doc://Event